  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. Skewness, as defined here, refers to the concentration of probability on unfavorable (lower) outcomes. For Lottery A: the unfavorable outcome is -6000 (45%) vs. 0 (55%). Since 0 is the better outcome, and it has 55% probability, more probability is on the favorable outcome — thus, Lottery A is left-skewed (not right-skewed). For Lottery B: the unfavorable outcome is -3000 (90%) vs. 0 (10%). Here, 90% of the probability is on the unfavorable outcome, meaning Lottery B is right-skewed. According to the decision reason, the more right-skewed lottery is preferred. Therefore, Lottery B is preferred by this reason. The relevant information — outcome magnitudes and their probabilities — is fully available, so the reason can be applied.",
