rable skew). Thus, the reason’s applicability is ambiguous, but technically, since A has a higher total probability of non-zero losses (50% vs 25%), it could be interpreted as more right-skewed in the loss domain. So the reason *can* be applied, and would prefer A if A is judged more right-skewed.",
